      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors That Affect the Price"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-off & Layers: Removing multiple old layers of shingles or heavy materials (like cedar shakes) adds labor and disposal fees."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch & Complexity: Steep slopes, multiple valleys, dormers, and chimney flashings make the job harder and more expensive."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Decking Repairs: Rotted or damaged plywood underneath the shingles will increase the bill if redecking is required."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Permits: Local building permits in Utah can add up to $500 depending on the municipality.",
